{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to propose a distributed requirement for a cross-cutting convention instead of marking each of its sites with `{impl}`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.bootstrap` has one obligation. The `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to propose a distributed requirement for a cross-cutting convention, rather than marking each site `{impl}`. Only a test that reads that skill's text and asserts the directive can check it.\n\n**Primary test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bootstrap_skill_proposes_distributed_requirements_for_conventions]` is marked `{test}` for the subject.\n- It reads the bootstrap skill's `SKILL.md` with `skill_md(\"habeas-bootstrap-requirements\")`.\n- It extracts the `## Proposing requirements` section with `section`.\n- It asserts with `assert_text` that the section contains \"propose a distributed requirement instead of marking each site `{impl}`\".\n- `assert_text` uses `assert!(text.contains(phrase))`, so a missing or reworded directive fails the test.\n- That phrase is the whole instruction the requirement states: propose a distributed requirement, not per-site `{impl}`.\n- The test scopes the check to the right skill and the right section, so the phrase cannot come from another skill or from unrelated text.\n\n**Supporting test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_refer_to_a_topic_home_instead_of_restating_it]` is also marked. For the bootstrap skill it asserts the referral to the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`. It also asserts that the skill does not restate other skills' home content. This adds a check that the guidance points to its topic home.\n\n**Cross-cutting condition.** The marked test does not assert the clause that scopes the directive to a convention applying at many sites. A different, unmarked test, `bundled_skills_say_when_to_read_each_reference_file`, asserts that clause in the bootstrap skill. The marked test still pins the directive itself, and I don't see a plausible violation that it would accept. If the skill dropped the directive or reversed it to per-site `{impl}`, the assertion would fail.\n\nI found no gap and no acknowledgments.",
